{"files": {"SKILL.md": "## Coding Execution Playbook\n\n### 1) Pre-change checks\n- Load the available docs, task context, and existing records before coding.\n- Mirror the request exactly; do not reinterpret requirements or add extras.\n\n### 2) Change strategy\n- Keep the patch minimal and localized to the requested target.\n- Reuse patterns from nearby code that already works before inventing a new approach.\n- Protect existing correct behavior while applying the fix.\n\n### 3) Tooling style\n- Favor a single chained terminal command when steps are sequential.\n- Read the full file first, then edit.\n\n### 4) Validation and handoff\n- Run relevant checks and treat results as the source of truth.\n- Re-verify the modified target after each meaningful change.\n- Communicate briefly and clearly.\n- When a persistent notes area exists, leave a short generalized takeaway.\n"}, "schema_version": 1}